<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $0.9 mln Sept 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $0.9 mln Sept 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $0.9 million deficit on September 25 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 25</p>
<p>Exports: $265 million</p>
<p>Imports: $202.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $294.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $357.6 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $0.9 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.810 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.950 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.940 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.427 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $373 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
